  "summary_of_core_decisions": "The text presents Kant's subjective universality as a normative, not empirical, claim. It resolves the paradox by grounding universal validity in the universal cognitive faculties of the subject, specifically through disinterestedness and free play. It defends against conflicting judgments by distinguishing actual psychological disagreement from normative requirements. It acknowledges limitations (unattainability, unfalsifiability, cultural pluralism) but concludes that the tension is the productive engine of aesthetic experience.",
